# This file should contain the SMTP password as a single line, with NO
# trailing newline if your swaks build is strict about it (most aren't).
# Permissions MUST be 600 and owner MUST be root. The orchestrator and
# every node read this file via `cat`.
#
# Example layout, for documentation only — replace with the real value:
#
#     replace-me-with-the-actual-smtp-password
#
# Recommended hardening (roadmap):
#   - move the secret into a HashiCorp Vault static secret, fetch with
#     short-lived token at run start, write into a tmpfs-backed file,
#     remove on exit.
#   - or: use a dedicated SMTP relay that only accepts authentication
#     from the orchestrator's static IP and only allows sending to a
#     short list of operator addresses.
